@host = https://ca-weatherimages-api.redbay-e7fc2782.norwayeast.azurecontainerapps.io

### 1. Start the image creation process. Returns a unique job id.
### The work runs in the background: two Container Apps Jobs are triggered by
### queue length (KEDA polls every 30 seconds). Allow about 2-3 minutes before
### all 40 images are in Blob Storage.
POST {{host}}/api/images

### 2. Fetch the status and the image links for the job started above.
### Paste the jobId from step 1 here.
### "Pending" with 0 images means the jobs have not finished yet - wait and retry.
GET {{host}}/api/images/PASTE-JOB-ID-HERE

### 3. A completed job from an earlier run, ready to inspect immediately.
GET {{host}}/api/images/ac626648-67b0-4c40-a68b-8991de53e889

### One of the generated images, served directly from Blob Storage.
GET https://stweatherimg707875.blob.core.windows.net/images/ac626648-67b0-4c40-a68b-8991de53e889/6215.png